.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-06-29T21:17:33Z","updated_at":"2026-06-30T14:58:31Z","closed_at":"2026-06-30T14:58:11Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.7.stable.official [5b4e0cb0f]\nv4.6.1.stable.official\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nAfter creating a canvas item via RenderingServer.canvas_item_create() with physics_interpolation = true produces wrong item position on appearance. This is due to the physics_interpolation that average between the two transforms but it is definetly not a desired behaviour as shown in the video below:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/24e73946-4d85-4edc-8dcd-9f6d11d42f48\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Put physics_interpolation = true\n- Create a canvas_item with RenderingServer.canvas_item_create()\n- Set the new canvas_item's parent and transform\n- To better notice the issue I suggest to continuosly add new canvas_items\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nJust run the only scene of the project to see the issue as shown in the video above.\nCircles are supposed to have their starting transform.origin at the tip of the arrow.\n\n[RenderingServerBugReport.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29481304/RenderingServerBugReport.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","follow